<hr data-start=3D"140" data-end=3D"143">
<h3 data-start=3D"145" data-end=3D"190"><strong data-start=3D"149" data-end=
=3D"190">Process Synchronization =E2=80=93 Explanation</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"192" data-end=3D"1027">
<li data-start=3D"192" data-end=3D"424">
<p data-start=3D"194" data-end=3D"424"><strong data-start=3D"194" data-end=
=3D"209">Definition:</strong><br data-start=3D"209" data-end=3D"212">
Process Synchronization is the technique of <strong data-start=3D"258" data=
-end=3D"310">coordinating the execution of multiple processes</strong> in s=
uch a way that <strong data-start=3D"330" data-end=3D"390">no two processes=
 access the shared data at the same time</strong>, to avoid <strong data-st=
art=3D"401" data-end=3D"423">data inconsistency</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"426" data-end=3D"846">
<p data-start=3D"428" data-end=3D"606"><strong data-start=3D"428" data-end=
=3D"449">Why it is Needed:</strong><br data-start=3D"449" data-end=3D"452">
In a <strong data-start=3D"459" data-end=3D"501">multiprocessing or multita=
sking system</strong>, several processes may run <strong data-start=3D"529"=
 data-end=3D"545">concurrently</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"550" data=
-end=3D"571">share common data</strong> (like variables, files, memory).</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"609" data-end=3D"846">
<li data-start=3D"609" data-end=3D"740">
<p data-start=3D"611" data-end=3D"740">If two or more processes try to <str=
ong data-start=3D"643" data-end=3D"684">read/write shared data simultaneous=
ly</strong>, the result may become <strong data-start=3D"708" data-end=3D"7=
37">inconsistent or incorrect</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"743" data-end=3D"846">
<p data-start=3D"745" data-end=3D"846">Example: Two processes updating a sh=
ared counter at the same time can overwrite each other=E2=80=99s changes.</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"848" data-end=3D"1027">
<p data-start=3D"850" data-end=3D"1027"><strong data-start=3D"850" data-end=
=3D"878">Goal of Synchronization:</strong><br data-start=3D"878" data-end=
=3D"881">
To make sure that when <strong data-start=3D"906" data-end=3D"963">one proc=
ess is accessing or modifying the shared data</strong>, <strong data-start=
=3D"965" data-end=3D"1000">other processes are not allowed</strong> to do s=
o at the same time.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1029" data-end=3D"1032">
<h3 data-start=3D"1034" data-end=3D"1066"><strong data-start=3D"1038" data-=
end=3D"1066">Critical Section Problem</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1068" data-end=3D"1658">
<li data-start=3D"1068" data-end=3D"1181">
<p data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1181">The part of the program where the =
<strong data-start=3D"1104" data-end=3D"1143">shared data is accessed or mo=
dified</strong> is called the <strong data-start=3D"1158" data-end=3D"1178"=
>Critical Section</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1182" data-end=3D"1658">
<p data-start=3D"1184" data-end=3D"1257">The <strong data-start=3D"1188" da=
ta-end=3D"1216">Critical Section Problem</strong> is to design a mechanism =
that ensures:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1260" data-end=3D"1658">
<li data-start=3D"1260" data-end=3D"1349">
<p data-start=3D"1263" data-end=3D"1349"><strong data-start=3D"1263" data-e=
nd=3D"1284">Mutual Exclusion:</strong> Only one process can be inside the c=
ritical section at a time.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1499">
<p data-start=3D"1355" data-end=3D"1499"><strong data-start=3D"1355" data-e=
nd=3D"1368">Progress:</strong> If no process is in the critical section, th=
en only the processes <strong data-start=3D"1435" data-end=3D"1455">waiting=
 to enter</strong> should decide who goes next =E2=80=94 not others.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1502" data-end=3D"1658">
<p data-start=3D"1505" data-end=3D"1658"><strong data-start=3D"1505" data-e=
nd=3D"1525">Bounded Waiting:</strong> There should be a <strong data-start=
=3D"1544" data-end=3D"1553">limit</strong> on how many times other processe=
s can enter the critical section before a waiting process gets its turn.</p=
>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1660" data-end=3D"1663">
<h3 data-start=3D"1665" data-end=3D"1699"><strong data-start=3D"1669" data-=
end=3D"1699">Synchronization Mechanisms</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1701" data-end=3D"1784">To solve the critical section prob=
lem, various synchronization mechanisms are used:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1786" data-end=3D"2116">
<li data-start=3D"1786" data-end=3D"1866">
<p data-start=3D"1789" data-end=3D"1814"><strong data-start=3D"1789" data-e=
nd=3D"1812">Software Solutions:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1818" data-end=3D"1866">
<li data-start=3D"1818" data-end=3D"1842">
<p data-start=3D"1820" data-end=3D"1842">Peterson=E2=80=99s Algorithm</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1846" data-end=3D"1866">
<p data-start=3D"1848" data-end=3D"1866">Bakery Algorithm</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1868" data-end=3D"1950">
<p data-start=3D"1871" data-end=3D"1896"><strong data-start=3D"1871" data-e=
