<hr data-start=3D"247" data-end=3D"250">
<h3 data-start=3D"252" data-end=3D"298"><strong data-start=3D"256" data-end=
=3D"298">Critical Section Problem =E2=80=93 Explanation</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"300" data-end=3D"1000">
<li data-start=3D"300" data-end=3D"457">
<p data-start=3D"302" data-end=3D"457">In a system with <strong data-start=
=3D"319" data-end=3D"334">n processes</strong> {P=E2=82=80, P=E2=82=81, =E2=
=80=A6, P=E2=82=99=E2=82=8B=E2=82=81}, these processes often <strong data-s=
tart=3D"376" data-end=3D"389">cooperate</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"=
394" data-end=3D"418">share data/resources</strong> like variables, files, =
or databases.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"458" data-end=3D"567">
<p data-start=3D"460" data-end=3D"567">A <strong data-start=3D"462" data-en=
d=3D"482">Critical Section</strong> is the part of the program where the pr=
ocess <strong data-start=3D"528" data-end=3D"564">accesses and updates shar=
ed data</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"568" data-end=3D"714">
<p data-start=3D"570" data-end=3D"714">If multiple processes <strong data-s=
tart=3D"592" data-end=3D"640">enter their critical sections simultaneously<=
/strong>, it can cause <strong data-start=3D"655" data-end=3D"677">data inc=
onsistency</strong> (also called <strong data-start=3D"691" data-end=3D"710=
">race conditions</strong>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"715" data-end=3D"835">
<p data-start=3D"717" data-end=3D"835">Therefore, the <strong data-start=3D=
"732" data-end=3D"752">main requirement</strong> is that <strong data-start=
=3D"761" data-end=3D"832">only one process should execute in its critical s=
ection at any time</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"836" data-end=3D"1000">
<p data-start=3D"838" data-end=3D"1000">The <strong data-start=3D"842" data=
-end=3D"876">Critical Section Problem (CSP)</strong> is to <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"883" data-end=3D"920">design a synchronization protocol</strong> so t=
hat processes can <strong data-start=3D"943" data-end=3D"967">share data co=
rrectly</strong> without causing inconsistencies.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1002" data-end=3D"1005">
<h3 data-start=3D"1007" data-end=3D"1036"><strong data-start=3D"1011" data-=
end=3D"1036">Sections of a Process</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1038" data-end=3D"1085">Each process can be divided into f=
our sections:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1087" data-end=3D"1620">
<li data-start=3D"1087" data-end=3D"1207">
<p data-start=3D"1090" data-end=3D"1110"><strong data-start=3D"1090" data-e=
nd=3D"1108">Entry Section:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1114" data-end=3D"1207">
<li data-start=3D"1114" data-end=3D"1207">
<p data-start=3D"1116" data-end=3D"1207">The part of the code where a proce=
ss <strong data-start=3D"1153" data-end=3D"1176">requests permission</stron=
g> to enter its critical section.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1209" data-end=3D"1338">
<p data-start=3D"1212" data-end=3D"1235"><strong data-start=3D"1212" data-e=
nd=3D"1233">Critical Section:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1338">
<li data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1338">
<p data-start=3D"1241" data-end=3D"1338">The part of the code where <strong=
 data-start=3D"1268" data-end=3D"1288">shared resources</strong> or <strong=
 data-start=3D"1292" data-end=3D"1312">shared variables</strong> are access=
ed or modified.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1340" data-end=3D"1498">
<p data-start=3D"1343" data-end=3D"1362"><strong data-start=3D"1343" data-e=
nd=3D"1360">Exit Section:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1498">
