<h2 data-start=3D"215" data-end=3D"261">=F0=9F=A7=A0 <strong data-start=3D"=
221" data-end=3D"261">Hardware Support for Synchronization</strong></h2>
<ul data-start=3D"263" data-end=3D"695">
<li data-start=3D"263" data-end=3D"491">
<p data-start=3D"265" data-end=3D"389"><strong data-start=3D"265" data-end=
=3D"309">Software-based synchronization solutions</strong> (like Peterson=
=E2=80=99s) may <strong data-start=3D"332" data-end=3D"351">not always work=
</strong> on <strong data-start=3D"355" data-end=3D"376">modern processors<=
/strong>, because of:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"392" data-end=3D"491">
<li data-start=3D"392" data-end=3D"441">
<p data-start=3D"394" data-end=3D"441"><strong data-start=3D"394" data-end=
=3D"420">Instruction reordering</strong> by compilers or CPUs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"444" data-end=3D"491">
<p data-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"491"><strong data-start=3D"446" data-end=
=3D"465">Cache coherence</strong> issues in multiprocessors</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"492" data-end=3D"695">
<p data-start=3D"494" data-end=3D"695">To overcome this, <strong data-start=
=3D"512" data-end=3D"583">modern computer architectures provide special har=
dware instructions</strong> that perform <strong data-start=3D"597" data-en=
d=3D"621">atomic (indivisible)</strong> operations to implement <strong dat=
a-start=3D"646" data-end=3D"666">mutual exclusion</strong> more easily and =
efficiently.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"697" data-end=3D"700">
<h3 data-start=3D"702" data-end=3D"740">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"708=
" data-end=3D"740">Common Hardware Instructions</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"742" data-end=3D"784">Two commonly used atomic instruction=
s are:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"786" data-end=3D"831">
<li data-start=3D"786" data-end=3D"807">
<p data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D"807"><code data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D=
"805">test_and_set()</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"808" data-end=3D"831">
<p data-start=3D"811" data-end=3D"831"><code data-start=3D"811" data-end=3D=
"831">compare_and_swap()</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote data-start=3D"833" data-end=3D"928">
<p data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"928">These instructions are <strong data-=
start=3D"858" data-end=3D"868">atomic</strong>, meaning they <strong data-s=
tart=3D"883" data-end=3D"927">execute as a single uninterruptible step</str=
ong>.</p>
</blockquote>
