<hr data-start=3D"2616" data-end=3D"2619">
<h2 data-start=3D"2621" data-end=3D"2659">=F0=9F=9F=A1 <strong data-start=
=3D"2627" data-end=3D"2659">Why Semaphores are Important</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"2661" data-end=3D"3021">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"26=
63" data-end=3D"2683">Mutual Exclusion</strong> =E2=80=93 Only one process =
enters critical section at a time (binary semaphore).<br data-start=3D"2756=
" data-end=3D"2759">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"2761" data-end=3D"2780">Synchronization</st=
rong> =E2=80=93 One process can signal another when a certain condition is =
true (e.g., producer-consumer).<br data-start=3D"2873" data-end=3D"2876">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"2878" data-end=3D"2924">No busy waiting (in=
 modern implementation)</strong> =E2=80=93 Instead of spinning, processes a=
re blocked and put into a waiting queue, which saves CPU time.</p>
