<hr data-start=3D"3352" data-end=3D"3355">
<h3 data-start=3D"3357" data-end=3D"3383"><strong data-start=3D"3361" data-=
end=3D"3383">Why this is better</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3384" data-end=3D"3503">
<li data-start=3D"3384" data-end=3D"3402">
<p data-start=3D"3386" data-end=3D"3402">No busy waiting.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3403" data-end=3D"3423">
<p data-start=3D"3405" data-end=3D"3423">CPU is not wasted.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3424" data-end=3D"3503">
<p data-start=3D"3426" data-end=3D"3503">Processes wait in a proper queue a=
nd are resumed when resources are released.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3505" data-end=3D"3508">
<h2 data-start=3D"3510" data-end=3D"3547">=F0=9F=9F=A1 <strong data-start=
=3D"3516" data-end=3D"3547">Key Points to Write in Exam</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"3549" data-end=3D"3812">=E2=9C=85 Semaphore definition and=
 origin (Dijkstra 1965)<br data-start=3D"3598" data-end=3D"3601">
=E2=9C=85 Atomic <code data-start=3D"3610" data-end=3D"3618">wait()</code> =
and <code data-start=3D"3623" data-end=3D"3633">signal()</code> operations<=
br data-start=3D"3644" data-end=3D"3647">
=E2=9C=85 Types: Binary &amp; Counting<br data-start=3D"3673" data-end=3D"3=
676">
=E2=9C=85 Usage pattern (wait before CS, signal after CS)<br data-start=3D"=
3725" data-end=3D"3728">
=E2=9C=85 Busy waiting problem<br data-start=3D"3750" data-end=3D"3753">
=E2=9C=85 Non-busy waiting solution with queue, block(), wakeup()</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3814" data-end=3D"3817">
<h2 data-start=3D"3819" data-end=3D"3852">=F0=9F=93=9D <strong data-start=
=3D"3825" data-end=3D"3852">Short 2=E2=80=933 Marks Version</strong></h2>
<blockquote data-start=3D"3854" data-end=3D"4272">
<p data-start=3D"3856" data-end=3D"4272">A <strong data-start=3D"3858" data=
-end=3D"3871">semaphore</strong> is an integer variable used for <strong da=
ta-start=3D"3904" data-end=3D"3931">process synchronization</strong>, intro=
duced by Dijkstra.<br data-start=3D"3956" data-end=3D"3959">
It=E2=80=99s accessed only through two atomic operations <code data-start=
=3D"4010" data-end=3D"4018">wait()</code> and <code data-start=3D"4023" dat=
a-end=3D"4033">signal()</code>.<br data-start=3D"4034" data-end=3D"4037">
Semaphores can be <strong data-start=3D"4057" data-end=3D"4067">binary</str=
ong> (0 or 1, for mutual exclusion) or <strong data-start=3D"4102" data-end=
=3D"4114">counting</strong> (for multiple resource instances).<br data-star=
t=3D"4149" data-end=3D"4152">
Basic implementation uses <strong data-start=3D"4180" data-end=3D"4196">bus=
y waiting</strong>, but advanced implementation uses <strong data-start=3D"=
4231" data-end=3D"4250">blocking queues</strong> to avoid CPU wastage.</p>
</blockquote>
