=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap">The Bounded-Buffer Problem(Producer=E2=80=93Consum=
er)
 Producer generates data items and puts them into a buffer.
 Consumer takes items from the buffer.
 The buffer has limited size (N slots).
 Constraints:
 =E2=80=A2 Producer must wait if buffer is full.
 =E2=80=A2 Consumer must wait if buffer is empty.
 =E2=80=A2 Mutual exclusion is required so two processes don=E2=80=99t upda=
te the buffer=20
simultaneously.
The Bounded-Buffer Problem using Semaphores
 Semaphores Used:
 We use three semaphores:
 semaphore mutex =3D 1;=20
semaphore empty =3D n;=20
semaphore full =3D 0
 mutex (binary semaphore)
 =E2=80=A2Ensures mutual exclusion when accessing buffer.
 empty (counting semaphore)
 =E2=80=A2Counts how many empty slots are available.
 full (counting semaphore)
 =E2=80=A2Counts how many slots are filled.
The Bounded-Buffer Problem
 The structure of the producer process:
     while (true) {=20
  wait(empty);=20
        wait(mutex);=20
...
     /* add item to the buffer */
 ...=20
        signal(mutex);=20
        signal(full);=20
     }
 =E2=80=A2Before inserting =E2=86=92 checks empty.
 =E2=80=A2 If no space (empty =3D=3D 0), producer blocks.
 =E2=80=A2Uses mutex to ensure only one producer/consumer=20
modifies buffer at a time.
 =E2=80=A2After inserting =E2=86=92 signals mutex and full.
The Bounded-Buffer Problem
 The structure of the Consumer process
     while (true) {=20
        wait(full);=20
        wait(mutex);=20
...
 /* take an item from buffer */
 ...=20
        signal(mutex);=20
        signal(empty);=20
     }
 =E2=80=A2Before removing =E2=86=92 checks full.=20
=E2=80=A2If no item (full =3D=3D 0), consumer blocks.
 =E2=80=A2Uses mutex for exclusive access.
