<h3 data-start=3D"2604" data-end=3D"2623">=F0=9F=94=8E Explanation:</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2917">
<li data-start=3D"2624" data-end=3D"2678">
<p data-start=3D"2627" data-end=3D"2678"><code data-start=3D"2627" data-end=
=3D"2639">wait(full)</code> =E2=86=92 Consumer waits if buffer is empty.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2679" data-end=3D"2738">
<p data-start=3D"2682" data-end=3D"2738"><code data-start=3D"2682" data-end=
=3D"2695">wait(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 Mutual exclusion for accessing buffe=
r.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2739" data-end=3D"2782">
<p data-start=3D"2742" data-end=3D"2782">Remove item =E2=86=92 safely take =
from buffer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2783" data-end=3D"2831">
<p data-start=3D"2786" data-end=3D"2831"><code data-start=3D"2786" data-end=
=3D"2801">signal(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 Release critical section.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2832" data-end=3D"2902">
<p data-start=3D"2835" data-end=3D"2902"><code data-start=3D"2835" data-end=
=3D"2850">signal(empty)</code> =E2=86=92 Tell producer there is <strong dat=
a-start=3D"2876" data-end=3D"2899">one more empty slot</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2903" data-end=3D"2917">
<p data-start=3D"2906" data-end=3D"2917">Use item.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"2919" data-end=3D"2922">
<h1 data-start=3D"2924" data-end=3D"2971">=F0=9F=9F=A1 How Deadlock / Race =
Condition is Prevented</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"2973" data-end=3D"3283">
<li data-start=3D"2973" data-end=3D"3200">
<p data-start=3D"2975" data-end=3D"3018"><strong data-start=3D"2975" data-e=
nd=3D"2998">Deadlock is avoided</strong> by proper ordering:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3021" data-end=3D"3200">
<li data-start=3D"3021" data-end=3D"3109">
<p data-start=3D"3023" data-end=3D"3109">Producer: <code data-start=3D"3033=
" data-end=3D"3046">wait(empty)</code> =E2=86=92 <code data-start=3D"3049" =
data-end=3D"3062">wait(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 insert =E2=86=92 <code data-=
start=3D"3074" data-end=3D"3089">signal(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 <code data-=
start=3D"3092" data-end=3D"3106">signal(full)</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3112" data-end=3D"3200">
<p data-start=3D"3114" data-end=3D"3200">Consumer: <code data-start=3D"3124=
" data-end=3D"3136">wait(full)</code> =E2=86=92 <code data-start=3D"3139" d=
ata-end=3D"3152">wait(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 remove =E2=86=92 <code data-s=
tart=3D"3164" data-end=3D"3179">signal(mutex)</code> =E2=86=92 <code data-s=
tart=3D"3182" data-end=3D"3197">signal(empty)</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3202" data-end=3D"3283">
<p data-start=3D"3204" data-end=3D"3283"><strong data-start=3D"3204" data-e=
nd=3D"3231">Race conditions avoided</strong> because only one process holds=
 <code data-start=3D"3263" data-end=3D"3270">mutex</code> at a time.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3285" data-end=3D"3288">
<h1 data-start=3D"3290" data-end=3D"3313">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Real-World Analogy</=
h1>
<p data-start=3D"3315" data-end=3D"3352">Imagine a <strong data-start=3D"33=
25" data-end=3D"3342">box of size N</strong> (buffer):</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3354" data-end=3D"3637">
<li data-start=3D"3354" data-end=3D"3421">
<p data-start=3D"3356" data-end=3D"3421"><strong data-start=3D"3356" data-e=
nd=3D"3375">Producer =3D Chef</strong> cooking food and putting plates in t=
he box.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3422" data-end=3D"3487">
<p data-start=3D"3424" data-end=3D"3487"><strong data-start=3D"3424" data-e=
nd=3D"3445">Consumer =3D Waiter</strong> taking plates and serving to custo=
mers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3488" data-end=3D"3523">
<p data-start=3D"3490" data-end=3D"3523"><strong data-start=3D"3490" data-e=
nd=3D"3513">empty =3D free spaces</strong> in box.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3524" data-end=3D"3560">
<p data-start=3D"3526" data-end=3D"3560"><strong data-start=3D"3526" data-e=
nd=3D"3550">full =3D filled spaces</strong> in box.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3561" data-end=3D"3637">
<p data-start=3D"3563" data-end=3D"3637"><strong data-start=3D"3563" data-e=
nd=3D"3634">mutex =3D only one person (chef or waiter) can open the box at =
a time</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3639" data-end=3D"3642">
<h1 data-start=3D"3644" data-end=3D"3668">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Variations in Exams<=
/h1>
<p data-start=3D"3670" data-end=3D"3778">In exams, they may twist the probl=
em into different scenarios, but the <strong data-start=3D"3741" data-end=
=3D"3767">core idea remains same</strong>. Examples:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"3780" data-end=3D"4296">
<li data-start=3D"3780" data-end=3D"3851">
<p data-start=3D"3783" data-end=3D"3851"><strong data-start=3D"3783" data-e=
nd=3D"3820">Single Producer &amp; Single Consumer</strong> (classic case we=
 explained).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3852" data-end=3D"3965">
<p data-start=3D"3855" data-end=3D"3965"><strong data-start=3D"3855" data-e=
nd=3D"3898">Multiple Producers &amp; Multiple Consumers</strong> =E2=86=92 =
still works fine because <code data-start=3D"3926" data-end=3D"3933">mutex<=
/code> ensures <strong data-start=3D"3942" data-end=3D"3962">mutual exclusi=
on</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3966" data-end=3D"4071">
<p data-start=3D"3969" data-end=3D"4071"><strong data-start=3D"3969" data-e=
nd=3D"3988">Buffer size =3D 1</strong> =E2=86=92 becomes the <strong data-s=
tart=3D"4003" data-end=3D"4068">Producer=E2=80=93Consumer with a single slo=
t (like ping-pong problem)</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4072" data-end=3D"4186">
<p data-start=3D"4075" data-end=3D"4186"><strong data-start=3D"4075" data-e=
nd=3D"4102">Priority-based Consumer</strong> =E2=86=92 sometimes the exam m=
ay ask what happens if consumers have different priorities.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4187" data-end=3D"4296">
<p data-start=3D"4190" data-end=3D"4296"><strong data-start=3D"4190" data-e=
nd=3D"4208">Removing mutex</strong> =E2=86=92 asked as a trap =E2=86=92 wit=
hout <code data-start=3D"4237" data-end=3D"4244">mutex</code>, multiple pro=
ducers/consumers can corrupt buffer.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"4298" data-end=3D"4301">
<h1 data-start=3D"4303" data-end=3D"4333">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Key Takeaways (for e=
xams)</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"4335" data-end=3D"4637">
<li data-start=3D"4335" data-end=3D"4385">
<p data-start=3D"4337" data-end=3D"4385"><strong data-start=3D"4337" data-e=
nd=3D"4357">Semaphores used:</strong> <code data-start=3D"4358" data-end=3D=
"4365">mutex</code>, <code data-start=3D"4367" data-end=3D"4374">empty</cod=
e>, <code data-start=3D"4376" data-end=3D"4382">full</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4386" data-end=3D"4432">
<p data-start=3D"4388" data-end=3D"4432"><strong data-start=3D"4388" data-e=
nd=3D"4430">Producer waits on empty, signals full.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4433" data-end=3D"4479">
<p data-start=3D"4435" data-end=3D"4479"><strong data-start=3D"4435" data-e=
nd=3D"4477">Consumer waits on full, signals empty.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4480" data-end=3D"4544">
<p data-start=3D"4482" data-end=3D"4544"><strong data-start=3D"4482" data-e=
nd=3D"4542">Mutex ensures only one process updates buffer at a time.</stron=
g></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4545" data-end=3D"4637">
<p data-start=3D"4547" data-end=3D"4637"><strong data-start=3D"4547" data-e=
nd=3D"4568">General structure</strong> is fixed =E2=86=92 even if the buffe=
r size or number of processes changes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4639" data-end=3D"4642">
<p data-start=3D"4644" data-end=3D"4661">=E2=9C=85 If you write:</p>
