<hr data-start=3D"4389" data-end=3D"4392">
<p data-start=3D"4394" data-end=3D"4445">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"43=
96" data-end=3D"4445">Quick summary for writing in exam (4=E2=80=935 lines)=
</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"4447" data-end=3D"4846">
<p data-start=3D"4449" data-end=3D"4846">The Readers-Writers problem deals =
with a shared database accessed by readers and writers.<br data-start=3D"45=
38" data-end=3D"4541">
Multiple readers can read simultaneously, but writers require exclusive acc=
ess.<br data-start=3D"4622" data-end=3D"4625">
Semaphores <code data-start=3D"4638" data-end=3D"4648">rw_mutex</code> and =
<code data-start=3D"4653" data-end=3D"4660">mutex</code> along with <code d=
ata-start=3D"4672" data-end=3D"4684">read_count</code> are used: first read=
er locks writers, last reader unlocks.<br data-start=3D"4743" data-end=3D"4=
746">
Writers lock <code data-start=3D"4761" data-end=3D"4771">rw_mutex</code> be=
fore writing. This ensures mutual exclusion and concurrency for readers.</p=
>
