t Readers-Writers strategy</strong> for a <strong data-start=3D"118" data-e=
nd=3D"151">real-time stock market system</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"156" data-end=3D"159">
<h1 data-start=3D"161" data-end=3D"181">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Problem Context</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"183" data-end=3D"440">
<li data-start=3D"183" data-end=3D"229">
<p data-start=3D"185" data-end=3D"229"><strong data-start=3D"185" data-end=
=3D"197">Scenario</strong>: Stock market analysis system</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"230" data-end=3D"303">
<p data-start=3D"232" data-end=3D"303"><strong data-start=3D"232" data-end=
=3D"243">Readers</strong>: Thousands of users viewing stock prices (high fr=
equency)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"304" data-end=3D"372">
<p data-start=3D"306" data-end=3D"372"><strong data-start=3D"306" data-end=
=3D"317">Writers</strong>: Few processes updating stock prices (low frequen=
cy)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"373" data-end=3D"440">
<p data-start=3D"375" data-end=3D"440"><strong data-start=3D"375" data-end=
=3D"383">Goal</strong>: Efficient, fair access to database =E2=86=92 avoid =
starvation</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"442" data-end=3D"445">
<h1 data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D"486">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Readers-Writers Soluti=
ons Overview</h1>
<ol data-start=3D"488" data-end=3D"1221">
<li data-start=3D"488" data-end=3D"729">
<p data-start=3D"491" data-end=3D"521"><strong data-start=3D"491" data-end=
=3D"519">Reader-Priority Solution</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"525" data-end=3D"729">
<li data-start=3D"525" data-end=3D"570">
<p data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"570">Multiple readers can access concurre=
ntly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"574" data-end=3D"620">
<p data-start=3D"576" data-end=3D"620">Writers wait until <strong data-star=
t=3D"595" data-end=3D"617">all readers finish</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"624" data-end=3D"729">
<p data-start=3D"626" data-end=3D"729"><strong data-start=3D"626" data-end=
=3D"637">Problem</strong>: Writers may <strong data-start=3D"651" data-end=
=3D"661">starve</strong> if there are always readers =E2=86=92 unacceptable=
 for real-time updates.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"731" data-end=3D"974">
<p data-start=3D"734" data-end=3D"764"><strong data-start=3D"734" data-end=
=3D"762">Writer-Priority Solution</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"768" data-end=3D"974">
<li data-start=3D"768" data-end=3D"825">
<p data-start=3D"770" data-end=3D"825">Writer gets <strong data-start=3D"78=
2" data-end=3D"794">priority</strong> whenever it requests access.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"829" data-end=3D"869">
<p data-start=3D"831" data-end=3D"869">Readers wait if a writer is waiting.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"873" data-end=3D"974">
<p data-start=3D"875" data-end=3D"974"><strong data-start=3D"875" data-end=
=3D"886">Problem</strong>: Readers may <strong data-start=3D"900" data-end=
=3D"910">starve</strong> if writers are frequent =E2=86=92 not ideal for th=
ousands of viewers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"976" data-end=3D"1221">
<p data-start=3D"979" data-end=3D"1015"><strong data-start=3D"979" data-end=
=3D"1013">Fair (or Alternating) Solution</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1019" data-end=3D"1221">
<li data-start=3D"1019" data-end=3D"1088">
<p data-start=3D"1021" data-end=3D"1088">Access granted in <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1039" data-end=3D"1059">order of arrival</strong> (first-come-first-s=
erved).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1092" data-end=3D"1145">
<p data-start=3D"1094" data-end=3D"1145">Ensures <strong data-start=3D"1102=
" data-end=3D"1119">no starvation</strong> for readers or writers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1149" data-end=3D"1221">
<p data-start=3D"1151" data-end=3D"1221">Slightly more complex but <strong =
data-start=3D"1177" data-end=3D"1218">best for systems with mixed workloads=
</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"1223" data-end=3D"1226">
<h1 data-start=3D"1228" data-end=3D"1274">=F0=9F=9F=A1 Suitable Solution fo=
r Stock Market System</h1>
<p data-start=3D"1276" data-end=3D"1318"><strong data-start=3D"1276" data-e=
nd=3D"1316">Fair (FIFO) Readers-Writers Solution</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1330"><strong data-start=3D"1320" data-e=
nd=3D"1328">Why?</strong></p>
<ol data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1840">
<li data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1436">
<p data-start=3D"1335" data-end=3D"1436"><strong data-start=3D"1335" data-e=
nd=3D"1355">Readers are many</strong>, but writes <strong data-start=3D"136=
8" data-end=3D"1402">cannot be delayed indefinitely</strong> =E2=86=92 stoc=
k prices must be updated.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1437" data-end=3D"1517">
<p data-start=3D"1440" data-end=3D"1517"><strong data-start=3D"1440" data-e=
nd=3D"1459">Writers are few</strong>, but must execute timely =E2=86=92 cri=
tical for real-time data.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1518" data-end=3D"1680">
<p data-start=3D"1521" data-end=3D"1544"><strong data-start=3D"1521" data-e=
nd=3D"1541">Fairness ensures</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1548" data-end=3D"1680">
<li data-start=3D"1548" data-end=3D"1624">
<p data-start=3D"1550" data-end=3D"1624">A writer gets access eventually ev=
en if thousands of readers are active.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1628" data-end=3D"1680">
<p data-start=3D"1630" data-end=3D"1680">Readers don=E2=80=99t starve while=
 writers are updating.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1681" data-end=3D"1840">
<p data-start=3D"1684" data-end=3D"1701"><strong data-start=3D"1684" data-e=
nd=3D"1698">Efficiency</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1705" data-end=3D"1840">
<li data-start=3D"1705" data-end=3D"1778">
<p data-start=3D"1707" data-end=3D"1778">Multiple readers can read <strong =
data-start=3D"1733" data-end=3D"1749">concurrently</strong> when no writer =
is waiting.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1782" data-end=3D"1840">
<p data-start=3D"1784" data-end=3D"1840">Writers block new readers temporar=
ily =E2=86=92 minimal delay.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
